  "historical_output_text": " I totally get your point that sometimes you need a higher priced product for durability. For a comparison that comes to the surface for many - it is between say buying the cheaper printer cartridge versus a high capacity cartridge or getting cheap coffee versus better-taste specialty coffee, it really all depends. While the initial outlay with higher capacity and specialty coffee products might look higher at checkout, there is often the long term trade offs and benefits you have not accounted. A lower initial spend with printer in cartridges, can result a need to buy replacements sooner which can cost as or cost more when averaged out per job or page over time.\nSimilarly specialty brew might seem pricey initially when you get the bulk coffee but in my experience over many brew cycles, you really notice a quality and flavor profile improvement and it just seems that much better with a little added spend.\nIn both scenarios",
